Python wrapper of xxhash that supports concurrency.

pyhashxx wraps the 32-bit xxHash non-cryptographic hash algorithm.  It
provides a convenience function, hashxx, that hashes the bytes of its
arguments (traversing tuples recursively), and a Hashxx class for
incremental hashing.  Unlike older wrappers it keeps no static global
hash context, so separate hash objects can be used concurrently.
